# Everything the build does not need, and everything it must never be given.
#
# The build context is the repository root — the Dockerfile copies each module's pom before its
# sources so a code change does not re-resolve dependencies. Without this file, `.env`, the mTLS
# private keys and every previously built jar are uploaded to the daemon on every build: slower,
# and a secret one layer away from being baked into an image.

# Secrets. Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/tls/
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.jks

# Build output. Rebuilt inside the image; copying it in invites a stale jar.
target/
**/target/

# Version control and editors.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# Documentation and samples. Nothing in the image reads them.
README.md
docs/
*.pdf
*.md
!contracts/**/*.md

# Local scratch.
*.log
scripts/
